---
export const prerender = true;
import '../../../styles/global.css';
import '../../../styles/cai-doc.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" />
  <title>The Baker's Dozen · AI Program · Cultivated AI</title>
  <style>
    /* ── At-a-glance map of the three workshops ── */
    .ses-map {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 0.7rem;
      margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    }
    .ses-mapcard {
      padding: 0.95rem 1.1rem 1.05rem;
      background: var(--color-warm-white);
      border: 1px solid rgba(26,26,46,0.07);
      border-radius: 8px;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .ses-mapcard::before {
      content: '';
      position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
      background: var(--bar);
    }
    .ses-mapcard .n {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.62rem; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--bar);
    }
    .ses-mapcard h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-heading);
      font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.08rem;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.15;
      margin: 0.15rem 0 0.35rem; color: var(--color-deep);
    }
    .ses-mapcard p {
      font-family: var(--font-body);
      font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.45;
      color: var(--color-subtle); margin: 0;
    }
    /* "Walk out with" note */
    .ses-out {
      margin: 1.4rem 0 0;
      padding: 0.95rem 1.25rem;
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bar, var(--color-navy)) 8%, var(--color-warm-white));
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--bar, var(--color-navy)) 28%, transparent);
      border-radius: 8px;
    }
    .ses-out h4 {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.64rem; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--bar, var(--color-navy)); margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    }
    .ses-out p {
      font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.55; color: var(--color-deep); margin: 0;
    }
    .ses-out p em { color: var(--color-navy); font-style: italic; }
    /* legend */
    .ses-legend {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem 0.6rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="cd-shell" style="--doc-accent: var(--color-navy);">

    <div class="cd-printhint screen-only">
      <span class="accent">Print to PDF →</span>
      Press <kbd>⌘ P</kbd> (or <kbd>Ctrl + P</kbd>), choose <strong>Save as PDF</strong>, background graphics <strong>on</strong>.
    </div>

    <p class="cd-eyebrow">Cultivated AI · The Baker's Dozen · program overview</p>
    <h1 class="cd-title">One goal, three <em>workshops</em></h1>
    <p class="cd-lede">The working shape of the engagement. <strong>Basics</strong> grounds the whole team in the same fifteen principles. <strong>Mission Control</strong> turns scattered dashboards into one place leadership can ask questions. <strong>Generative Media Bootcamp</strong> takes the marketing team hands-on with image, video, music and voice. Twelve live hours, and every session ends in something you keep.</p>
    <p class="cd-meta">Three workshops · six sessions × 2 hrs · one data-room prep · The Baker's Dozen</p>
    <div class="cd-rule"></div>

    <div class="ses-map">
      <div class="ses-mapcard is-amber" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
        <span class="n">Workshop 1 · 2 × 2 hrs</span>
        <h3>Basics · Cultivated AI</h3>
        <p>The starter workshop: how AI works and the fifteen principles, all hands-on. For the wider team.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ses-mapcard is-sky" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
        <span class="n">Workshop 2 · prep + 2 × 2 hrs</span>
        <h3>Mission Control</h3>
        <p>A data room leadership can question in plain language. Leaders and data owners.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ses-mapcard is-red" style="--bar: var(--color-accent-red);">
        <span class="n">Workshop 3 · 2 × 2 hrs</span>
        <h3>Generative Media Bootcamp</h3>
        <p>Hands-on with image, video, music and voice tools, in the brand's own taste. For the marketing, content and branding team.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ════════ WORKSHOP 01 ════════ -->
    <section class="cd-section is-amber" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Workshop 01</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">Basics · <em>Cultivated AI</em></h2>
        <span class="cd-section-aside">2 sessions × 2 hrs</span>
      </div>
      <p class="cd-section-blurb">The starter discipline, for the wider team. No coding and no prior AI experience needed. Bring a laptop, Chrome, and three tasks you repeat every week.</p>

      <div class="cd-callout" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
        <h4>Objective</h4>
        <p>Everyone leaves speaking the same language about AI, with the fifteen principles applied to their own work on their own keyboard.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="cd-timeline" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
        <li class="cd-beat"><span class="cd-beat-time">S1 · 2 hrs</span><div class="cd-beat-body">
          <p class="cd-beat-name">How it works, and what's out there</p>
          <p class="cd-beat-desc">Why AI matters, and why your job is safe with you in the loop. How these models behave, learned through live experiments with prompts, tokens, context and slop. Then the map: which tools are good at what, from chat to image, video and music.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-beat"><span class="cd-beat-time">S2 · 2 hrs</span><div class="cd-beat-body">
          <p class="cd-beat-name">Agents, skills and a plan</p>
          <p class="cd-beat-desc">Everyone builds a working browser extension. A tour of what agents like Claude Code can carry. Skills: saving your best methods and sharing them with the team. Closes with each person starting their 90-day plan.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="ses-out" style="--bar: var(--color-amber);">
        <h4>Walk out with</h4>
        <p>A de-slop prompt in your own voice · a browser extension you built · a starter skill · a 90-day plan underway.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ════════ WORKSHOP 02 ════════ -->
    <section class="cd-section is-sky" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Workshop 02</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">Mission <em>Control</em></h2>
        <span class="cd-section-aside">prep + 2 sessions × 2 hrs</span>
      </div>
      <p class="cd-section-blurb">One place to ask the business a question and get an answer you can act on. A smaller cohort: the leaders who ask the questions and the people who own the data. Showing up in AI answers (AEO) rides along at the end as a bonus.</p>

      <div class="cd-callout" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
        <h4>The data room · before any session</h4>
        <p>This one needs no cohort, only read access. With Power BI, GobbleCube exports, production and supply chain data on the table, we sit with the data owner and build: the warehouse, the daily dump, the first queries. Session 1 then starts with a data room that already works. We build with Claude Code, so the company will need a Claude Max plan.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="cd-timeline" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
        <li class="cd-beat"><span class="cd-beat-time">S1 · 2 hrs</span><div class="cd-beat-body">
          <p class="cd-beat-name">Answers you can trust</p>
          <p class="cd-beat-desc">The metric dictionary: defining the company's words so answers always mean the same thing, plus the honesty rules that stop made-up numbers. Golden questions, then free play in the data room.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-beat"><span class="cd-beat-time">S2 · 2 hrs</span><div class="cd-beat-body">
          <p class="cd-beat-name">Putting it to work</p>
          <p class="cd-beat-desc">One real problem worked from question to decision. A custom dashboard built live with Claude Code. An answer key that scores the system monthly. Roadmap, owner, and a bonus look at showing up in AI answers.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="ses-out" style="--bar: var(--color-sky);">
        <h4>Walk out with</h4>
        <p>A data room refreshed daily · a metric dictionary · a dashboard the team built · a monthly answer-key score · a roadmap with an owner.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ════════ WORKSHOP 03 ════════ -->
    <section class="cd-section is-red" style="--bar: var(--color-accent-red);">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Workshop 03</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">Generative Media <em>Bootcamp</em></h2>
        <span class="cd-section-aside">2 sessions × 2 hrs</span>
      </div>
      <p class="cd-section-blurb">Built from the branding team's own expectation list, and tuned by their questionnaire answers. Hands-on with the brand's real briefs, calendar and accounts.</p>

      <div class="cd-callout" style="--bar: var(--color-accent-red);">
        <h4>Objective</h4>
        <p>A marketing team that makes image, video, music and voice at AI speed, in a voice that still sounds like The Baker's Dozen.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="cd-timeline" style="--bar: var(--color-accent-red);">
        <li class="cd-beat"><span class="cd-beat-time">S1 · 2 hrs</span><div class="cd-beat-body">
          <p class="cd-beat-name">Taste, voice and the tools</p>
          <p class="cd-beat-desc">The gen media map and how prompting changes per medium. Brand voice, and when not to use AI at all. The Baker's Dozen bible and the taste recipe book get started in the room.</p>
        </div></li>
        <li class="cd-beat"><span class="cd-beat-time">S2 · 2 hrs</span><div class="cd-beat-body">
          <p class="cd-beat-name">Making things</p>
          <p class="cd-beat-desc">A content calendar that maintains itself in Claude. Images and video made on real briefs. Motion graphics overlays and edits with Claude Code. Music and voice, plus deep research on the brand and its competitors.</p>
        </div></li>
      </ol>

      <div class="ses-out" style="--bar: var(--color-accent-red);">
        <h4>Walk out with</h4>
        <p>The bible and recipe book started · a voice kit that de-slops everything · a calendar living in Claude · real work made on real briefs.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ════════ How we start ════════ -->
    <section class="cd-section is-navy">
      <div class="cd-section-rule"></div>
      <div class="cd-section-head">
        <span class="cd-section-num">Next</span>
        <h2 class="cd-section-name">How we <em>start</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cd-prose">
        <p><strong>Questionnaires first.</strong> Each track has its own pre-work: the ten-question interview for Basics, the eighteen-question data interview for Mission Control, and a short brief-collection form for the brand team. Answers shape the sessions before anyone walks in.</p>
        <p><strong>Prep in parallel.</strong> The Mission Control data room starts the moment access is granted. It does not wait for scheduling, so by the time the cohort sits down the warehouse is already answering.</p>
        <p><strong>Then schedule.</strong> Basics runs first so every later session lands on shared ground. Mission Control and Generative Media Bootcamp can run in either order, or interleaved week by week.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="cd-footer">
      <span class="brand">Cultivated AI · <em>Grow, don't Chase.</em></span>
      <span>The Baker's Dozen · program overview</span>
    </div>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
